 **Why.** Six of the ten workstreams reported new SQL they could not run against Postgres (no `NEON_URL` in a worktree), and `rejected.md#offline-mocks-cannot-type-check-sql` is exactly the failure a plan-only EXPLAIN catches for free: WS-R172's agent mint (four write nodes, cost 236), WS-R175's erasure chain (116 delete nodes including the six newly ordered ones, cost 1310), WS-R173's card read, WS-R179's two reads and WS-R180's sheet read all planned first time. The marker rule exists because a follow-up commit that rewrites its own earlier paragraph is a legitimate thing for a workstream to do and the union tool refuses it correctly; the failure was the main loop chaining `git add` behind the refusal.
 
 **Reversal.** If a plan-only EXPLAIN ever passes a statement that then fails live (a runtime-only error such as a constraint the plan cannot see), the live apply of a seeded fixture becomes the merge-time check for write statements; if a context-union refusal is ever resolved wrongly by hand twice in one wave, the union tool gains a `--replace-paragraph` mode instead.
+
+## `ws-r182-owner-memory-consolidation-wired-through-the-shared-metered-sweep` (2026-09-14, WS-R182)
+
+**Decision.** Supersedes `#ws-r167-owner-memory-consolidation-left-unmetered`
+by name, doing exactly what that entry's own reversal condition asked for.
+Three additive pieces, no fork of anything WS-R167 built:
+
+1. **The write that never existed.** `generateOwnedTextDialogue`
+   (`api/_replica-dialogue.js`) never wrote the owner's own message to
+   `meera_log` at all — the voice-ready path's own writer
+   (`PRIVATE_DIALOGUE_BEGIN_SQL`) is FK-bound to
+   `vy_replica_runtime_capability`, which a text-ready-only replica has
+   none of, and nothing else ever ran in its place. So `OWNER_MEMORY_BATCH_
+   SQL` (WS-R167) always found zero rows regardless of whether anything
+   scheduled it — the gap was one layer deeper than "unmetered." A new
+   statement, `OWNER_MEMORY_LOG_SQL` (`api/_room-memory-authority.js`),
+   closes it: one `with` block that self-ensures a `vy_person_device`
+   mapping (via a NEW deterministic synthetic device id, `ownerMeetDeviceId`,
+   the identical RFC 4122 §4.3 v5 technique `api/_room.js#surfaceDeviceId`
+   already uses, reproduced independently rather than imported — importing
+   a Room module into the owner's own private lane would be exactly the
+   "person-facing Room-shaped detour" WS-R167's own law 3 forbids) and then
+   logs the `role='me'` row, re-deriving `agent_id`/`person_id` from
+   `OWNER_MEMORY_AUTHORITY` exactly like every other statement in that
+   section — never a client-supplied id. Called from `generateOwnedTextDialogue`
+   AFTER `generator.generate()` succeeds (the turn's own "commit" point),
+   awaited, not fire-and-forget: `#trace-off-path`'s own measured law —
+   "a serverless function that has already responded cannot be relied on to
+   finish work" — rules out doing this after the response goes out, so this
+   one cheap INSERT rides the same request that already pays for the LLM call.
+2. **Discovery.** `OWNER_MEMORY_DISCOVERY_SQL` (new): the sweep's own
+   candidate list, one statement, the same global oldest-first shape
+   `ROOM_MEMORY_DISCOVERY_SQL` already is. An owner never appears in it
+   without an active, unrevoked `'memory'`-scope consent grant — the SAME
+   "their choice is the predicate" discipline the rest of the owner-memory
+   section already rests on — so memory OFF means no consolidation is ever
+   scheduled, proven with a negative control (`evals/meet-continuity`,
+   `evals/room-leak` layer 19 addendum).
+3. **Dispatch.** `runMeteredRoomMemoryConsolidation`
+   (`api/_room-memory-consolidation.js`) gains the SAME five optional
+   parameters (`batchSql`/`commitSql`/`batchParams`/`authorityOf`/
+   `sourceBindingFn`/`extractionSystem`/`adapterVersion`, all defaulting to
+   Room's own exact shape so every existing caller is byte-identical) the
+   unmetered `runRoomMemoryConsolidation` already carries — WS-R167's own
+   header previewed this exact extension. `runMeteredOwnerMemoryConsolidation`
+   calls it with the owner's own SQL/authority/extraction prompt. Nothing
+   about the lease (`meera_consolidate_lease`, keyed by `(agent_id,
+   person_id)` alone, already generic), the provider-budget reservation/
+   settle path, or the exact-source-reread CAS in `runMeteredRoomMemoryModel`
+   changed at all — the owner lane runs through literally the same code.
+   `api/consolidate-sweep.js`'s `room_only` mode now also discovers owner
+   candidates (`OWNER_MEMORY_DISCOVERY_SQL`) and dispatches each one tagged
+   `lane:'owner'` through `runMeteredOwnerMemoryConsolidation` — inserted as
+   a NEW branch checked and returned BEFORE the existing `if (roomOnly)`
+   Room block, which stays byte-identical (so `evals/agent/raw-isolation.mjs`'s
+   and `evals/incidents/run.mjs`'s own source-regex negative controls on that
+   exact block are unaffected). Never a third `SWEEP_MODE`, never a second
+   cron.
+
+**The scheduling choice — sweep discovery, never fire-after-respond.** The
+brief's own two options were "fire after respond, or the sweep door picks it
+up on its next tick." `#trace-off-path`'s own measured law above settles
+it: a fire-and-forget promise started after the HTTP response goes out can
+be frozen by the platform mid-flight on Vercel, and nothing in this repo has
+ever relied on that working (`api/chat.js`, `api/_gcache.js`,
+`api/account.js` all name the same lesson for their own on-path writes).
+The sweep, already the ONLY thing that will ever run Room memory unattended
+(`api/consolidate-sweep.js`'s own header), is the proven shape.
+
+**Why.** WS-R167 left the reversal condition explicit: "a future workstream
+can extend `runMeteredRoomMemoryConsolidation`'s own five new optional
+parameters to point at `OWNER_MEMORY_BATCH_SQL`/`OWNER_MEMORY_COMMIT_SQL`/
+`ownerMemoryAuthority` with no structural rework." That is exactly what this
+workstream did, plus the raw write and discovery a scheduler needs before it
+has anything to consolidate at all — neither of which WS-R167 built or
+claimed to.
+
+**Reversal.** If a future measurement shows the sweep's own hourly/hand-
+triggered cadence is too slow for the owner's own Meet (a person noticing
+their AI "forgets" minutes-old context across a session), the fire-after-
+respond alternative should be reconsidered ONLY once the runtime gains a
+reliable `waitUntil` (`#trace-off-path`'s own reversal condition,
+unchanged) — never before, since nothing in this environment can prove a
+fire-and-forget write survives today. If `ownerMeetDeviceId`'s deterministic
+seed is ever found to collide with a real `api/_room.js` surface seed (it
+cannot, by construction — disjoint fixed prefixes, `meet:` vs `tg:`/`dm:` —
+but if evidence ever shows otherwise), the two id spaces need an explicit
+namespace separator rather than relying on prefix distinctness alone.
+
+**No migration.** `172` (reserved for this workstream) was not needed: no
+new table. `vy_person_device` already exists and is already agent-independent
+(`context/decisions.md` line ~5947's own established law); `meera_consolidate_
+lease` was already generic across both lanes; erasure/export already reach
+both `meera_log` and `vy_person_device` through the existing generic,
+device-keyed `PERSON_TABLES` scan (`api/memory.js`) — no new cascade code.
